(Fernbrook Labs Policy DRP-3: Data Retention and Deletion) Tj T*
T*
(Version 2.1. Owner: Security and Compliance. Applies to all Wayline production systems in every) Tj T*
(region.) Tj T*
T*
(1. Purpose and scope) Tj T*
T*
(We keep customer data only as long as we need it to run the service, meet legal obligations and) Tj T*
(recover from failures. This policy states how long each kind of data is kept and how it is) Tj T*
(deleted. It applies to prod-us2 and prod-eu1, and to every copy of production data, including) Tj T*
(restore points and logs.) Tj T*
T*
(2. Retention schedule) Tj T*
T*
(Event payloads: 30 days after the event is published. This also applies to deliveries in the) Tj T*
(dead-letter queue.) Tj T*
(Delivery attempt records \(status codes, response times, error messages\): 90 days.) Tj T*
(Audit logs of account and configuration changes: 400 days.) Tj T*
(Database snapshots: a restore point is taken every 6 hours and each one is kept for 35 days.) Tj T*
(Billing and invoicing records: 7 years, as required by tax law.) Tj T*
T*
(Data is deleted automatically when its retention period ends. Monthly partitions are dropped as) Tj T*
(a whole rather than deleted row by row.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
