(3. Customer requests) Tj T*
T*
(When a customer closes their account, all of their data is deleted from live systems within 30) Tj T*
(days.) Tj T*
T*
(Requests to erase the personal data of an individual are completed within 30 days of being) Tj T*
(verified. Restore points are immutable and are never edited to remove a single record. Erased) Tj T*
(data can therefore remain inside existing restore points until they expire, which happens at) Tj T*
(most 35 days later. If we ever restore from such a restore point, erasure requests are) Tj T*
(re-applied before the restored system serves traffic.) Tj T*
T*
(4. Recovery objectives) Tj T*
T*
(Our recovery point objective \(RPO\) is 6 hours, matching the snapshot interval. Our recovery) Tj T*
(time objective \(RTO\) is 4 hours. The infrastructure team runs a full restore drill every) Tj T*
(quarter and records the measured restore time.) Tj T*
T*
(5. Legal holds) Tj T*
T*
(A legal hold suspends deletion for the data it covers until the hold is lifted by the legal) Tj T*
(team. Data under a legal hold is still access-controlled as described in SEC-01.) Tj T*
T*
(6. Review) Tj T*
T*
(This policy is reviewed once a year by Security and Compliance.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
